    "messageType": "Update",
    "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...Northwestern Brevard County in east central Florida...\nSoutheastern Orange County in east central Florida...\n\n* WHEN...Until 900 PM EST.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 648 PM EST, Automated traffic cameras showed flooding in the\nwarned area. Flooding is already occurring. Between 3 and 7\ninches of rain have fallen.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nWedgefield, Christmas, Lone Cabbage Fish Camp and Bithlo.\n- Water is over the roadway on FL-520 at the intersection with the\nBeachline (FL-528).\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
