    "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Most of east central Florida, including Volusia, Seminole,\nOrange, Osceola, Okeechobee, Brevard, Indian River, Saint Lucie,\nand Martin counties.\n\n* WHEN...From Tuesday afternoon through Friday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Repeated rounds of showers and isolated storms are forecast\nthrough Friday. Rainfall amounts of 3 to 6 inches are forecast\nwith localized higher amounts of 8 to 12 inches. The greatest\npotential for these higher amounts will be over the coastal\ncounties.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
